{
 "protocol": " Post-sprint step 3 (Yotam 11-28): invariance evals on frozen checkpoints (no training).\n\nClips (never used to train any student; the students train on paired v2 [0, 12000) only):\n  U = unpaired8: 12,000 of its 25,000 scenes (RandomState(0)), one clip per scene = one room per clip, 113 WSJ0 speakers\n      (~106 clips each); first 65,792 samples (4.112 s, the training length) of the 8.2-s clips.\n  P = paired v2 held-out scenes [12000, 12500) x 4 renderings (2,000 clips; 500 rooms, 4 different speakers per room).\n      Caveat: every held-out utterance also occurs (in other rooms) in the training scenes, and it is small (~9 SID\n      training clips per speaker).\nEmbedding per encoder: STFTLearner.data_preprocess -> JointSpatialDownstream(concat).patches -> mean over patches (768-d),\n  exactly what ridge_dump / the lineareval head see. Probes: ridge, standard protocol (z-score, 33 lambdas, 5-fold CV;\n  rir_encoder.ridge_cv for regression, teacher_geometry.ridge_cv(classify=True) for SID = one-hot ridge, argmax).\nEvals:\n  1 cross-speaker room estimation (U; TDOA samples / T60 s / DRR dB / C50 dB MAE): speakers split in two halves\n    (RandomState(1)); cross = train on half a, test on half b (both directions); reference = a random clip split with the\n    same train / test sizes (speakers shared), per direction. Headline = mean over directions of (cross - random) MAE.\n  2 cross-room SID (U; linear SID accuracy %): clips split at the median T60, and at the median DRR; cross = train on one\n    half, test on the other (both directions, both factors: 4 splits); reference = random clip split of the same sizes.\n    Headline = mean over the 4 of (cross - random) accuracy.\n  3 secondary (P): SID seen-room (each room: renderings 0, 1 train, 2, 3 test) vs unseen-room (rooms 12000-12249 train,\n    12250-12499 test); test clips whose speaker has no training clip are dropped (count reported).\nBoth encoders on every eval: spatial = the room-estimation encoder, spectral = the SID encoder; the other = leakage rows.\n",
 "n_U": 12000,
 "n_P": 2000,
